<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Gottorp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1768">1768</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Gottorp Settlement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Gottorp, concluded in 1768, settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>'s long dispute with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, whose kings as dukes of Holstein had claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the city. Denmark recognised Hamburg as a free imperial city in return for financial concessions by the city. It ended the threat of Danish annexation that had hung over Hamburg since the 16th century.</p></div>
